                                                                                                                <comments>
                            <comment id="15427534" author="anovikov" created="Fri, 19 Aug 2016 03:09:55 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Fixed split for range under mysql dialect. Add warning on error.&lt;br/&gt;
Alexey^ please review.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15427548" author="kuaw26" created="Fri, 19 Aug 2016 03:24:19 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Pavel please test, that data will load correctly from MySQL and also do some sort of load test, load for example 50_000_000 rows.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;And check that most popular RDBMS (DB2, Oracle, Postgress, ...) also support parallel load.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15427995" author="pkonstantinov" created="Fri, 19 Aug 2016 11:00:14 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Created a test project and database with table with 21 million of rows.&lt;br/&gt;
Test grid with only one node with 9 GB of heap.&lt;br/&gt;
Cache has OFFHEAP mode.&lt;br/&gt;
I was able to load maximum 10 millions of row.&lt;br/&gt;
It seems that MySQL driver fetching all result set in heap.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Attaching the test project.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15430256" author="pkonstantinov" created="Mon, 22 Aug 2016 07:51:18 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Successfully tested in branch - I was able to load 21M of rows during 6 min.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15430276" author="kuaw26" created="Mon, 22 Aug 2016 08:10:20 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Fixed MySQL loading large result sets. Merged to master.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15430354" author="pkonstantinov" created="Mon, 22 Aug 2016 09:00:08 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Successfully re-tested in master.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
